ssir_dump
=========

A standalone decoder for the SsIr.bin IR database carried in the userconfig
region of a zwave usbnet Harmony remote (1000/1100/...). It walks the tail
index, finds each device/sequence Press signal, detects the protocol from the
pulse timing, and prints the decoded code.

The on-disk format and the pulse encoding are documented in
../specs/ir_database.txt.

BUILD

    make
    (or: cc -O2 -Wall -o ssir_dump ssir_dump.c)

USAGE

Dump a remote's config first (see the top-level README), unzip the EZHex's
inner PK zip, and point the tool at userconfig/SsIr.bin:

    ssir_dump SsIr.bin

Output is one line per device/sequence, e.g.:

    # device 0  (74 sequences)
      dev 0 seq 0   : NEC addr=0x0707 cmd=0x99
    # device 4  (57 sequences)
      dev 4 seq 0   : RC6 mode=6 customer=0x800F cmd=0x24
    # device 5  (22 sequences)
      dev 5 seq 0   : PD 112-bit: 11 11 11 11 11 24 03 09 04 ... 89 (chk ok)

RECOGNISED PROTOCOLS

    NEC / extended-NEC, RC6 mode 6A (MCE / eHome), a pulse-distance AC frame
    (with a sum-mod-256 checksum), and a fixed-mark / quantized-gap scheme seen
    on a PVR remote. Learned (ircap) or unrecognised signals are reported with
    their raw lead-in timing rather than guessed.

This decodes the stored mark/space timings; it does not talk to a remote.
